-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore), G.N. No. S 914/2021, current version as at 5 November 2026.
-- ORDER 19 (part roc4), DIVISION 3 -- APPEALS FROM GENERAL DIVISION TO APPELLATE DIVISION OR COURT OF APPEAL, ETC.
-- (rules 24 to 40), LAYER 1: the law, objectively.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from Singapore Statutes Online.
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here has been checked against the official text.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT, and the time seams: as in roc4-order-19-div-1.l4 (imported).
-- Each function is named for the provision's own proposition (the duty, the bar, the power).
-- The Supreme Court of Judicature Act is not among the sources: its sections 29B, 29C, 29D, 29E, 40, 47 and 58 and its Sixth Schedule are borrowed facts, asked as inputs named for the section.
-- Division 5 of Order 18 (roc3's range) is not encoded here: rules 28 and 29 only say that it may apply instead.
-- Rule 29 switches this Division off for an appeal; per PLAN.md section 5 (S-L2) the other rules of this Division do not thread an input for it.

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 19 -- Division 3 -- Appeals from General Division to Appellate Division or Court of Appeal, etc.`
-- ===========================================================================

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 24 -- scope of this Division`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:2496 | 24. This Division applies to — ( a )
-- src:2497 | an appeal to the Appellate Division against a judgment of the General Division (including an appeal transferred between the Appellate Division and the Court of Appeal);
-- src:2498 | ( b )
-- src:2499 | an appeal to the Court of Appeal against a judgment of the General Division (including an appeal transferred between the Appellate Division and the Court of Appeal);
-- src:2500 | ( c )
-- src:2501 | an appeal to the Court of Appeal against a judgment of the Appellate Division;
-- src:2502 | ( d )
-- src:2503 | an application to the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal relating to an appeal mentioned in paragraph ( a ), ( b ) or ( c ); and
-- src:2504 | ( e )
-- src:2505 | an appeal from any tribunal to the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal pursuant to any written law, subject to such modifications as may be directed by the appellate Court.
@ref O 19 r 24 (src:2496-2505)
GIVEN route IS A `o 19 r 2 route of appeal`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 24(a) this Division applies to an appeal to the Appellate Division against a judgment of the General Division` MEANS
    IF       NOT (route's `o 19 r 2 from a tribunal`)
        AND  NOT (route's `o 19 r 2 from a Disciplinary Tribunal under the Medical Registration Act`)
        AND  route's `o 19 r 2 appealed from` EQUALS `General Division`
        AND  route's `o 19 r 2 appealed to` EQUALS `Appellate Division`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): rule 24 lists five kinds and does not say "only"

@ref O 19 r 24(b) (src:2498-2499)
GIVEN route IS A `o 19 r 2 route of appeal`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 24(b) this Division applies to an appeal to the Court of Appeal against a judgment of the General Division` MEANS
    IF       NOT (route's `o 19 r 2 from a tribunal`)
        AND  NOT (route's `o 19 r 2 from a Disciplinary Tribunal under the Medical Registration Act`)
        AND  route's `o 19 r 2 appealed from` EQUALS `General Division`
        AND  route's `o 19 r 2 appealed to` EQUALS `Court of Appeal`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): rule 24 lists five kinds and does not say "only"

@ref O 19 r 24(c) (src:2500-2501)
GIVEN route IS A `o 19 r 2 route of appeal`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 24(c) this Division applies to an appeal to the Court of Appeal against a judgment of the Appellate Division` MEANS
    IF       NOT (route's `o 19 r 2 from a tribunal`)
        AND  route's `o 19 r 2 appealed from` EQUALS `Appellate Division`
        AND  route's `o 19 r 2 appealed to` EQUALS `Court of Appeal`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): rule 24 lists five kinds and does not say "only"

@ref O 19 r 24(d) (src:2502-2503)
GIVEN `the application is to the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it relates to an appeal mentioned in paragraph (a), (b) or (c)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 24(d) this Division applies to an application to the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal relating to an appeal` MEANS
    IF `the application is to the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal` AND `it relates to an appeal mentioned in paragraph (a), (b) or (c)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): rule 24 lists five kinds and does not say "only"

@ref O 19 r 24(e) (src:2504-2505)
GIVEN route IS A `o 19 r 2 route of appeal`
      `the appeal is pursuant to a written law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 24(e) this Division applies to an appeal from a tribunal to the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal` MEANS
    IF       route's `o 19 r 2 from a tribunal`
        AND (   route's `o 19 r 2 appealed to` EQUALS `Appellate Division`
             OR route's `o 19 r 2 appealed to` EQUALS `Court of Appeal`)
        AND  `the appeal is pursuant to a written law`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): rule 24 lists five kinds and does not say "only"

-- "subject to such modifications as may be directed by the appellate Court": a direction is outside the text.
@ref O 19 r 24(e) (src:2504-2505)
GIVEN `the appellate Court has directed modifications` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 24(e) this Division applies to the tribunal appeal without modification` MEANS
    IF `the appellate Court has directed modifications`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "subject to such modifications as may be directed by the appellate Court" -- the direction is not in these sources
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- Gathered by hand (option B of ruling E1, guidance only).
@ref O 19 r 24 (src:2496-2505)
GIVEN route IS A `o 19 r 2 route of appeal`
      `the application is to the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it relates to an appeal mentioned in paragraph (a), (b) or (c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appeal is pursuant to a written law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 24 this Division applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `o 19 r 24(a) this Division applies to an appeal to the Appellate Division against a judgment of the General Division` route EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `o 19 r 24(b) this Division applies to an appeal to the Court of Appeal against a judgment of the General Division` route EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `o 19 r 24(c) this Division applies to an appeal to the Court of Appeal against a judgment of the Appellate Division` route EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `o 19 r 24(d) this Division applies to an application to the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal relating to an appeal` `the application is to the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal` `it relates to an appeal mentioned in paragraph (a), (b) or (c)` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `o 19 r 24(e) this Division applies to an appeal from a tribunal to the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal` route `the appeal is pursuant to a written law` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): rule 24 lists five kinds and does not say "only"

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 25 -- bringing of appeal`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

`o 19 r 25(1)(a) the period for the notice of appeal` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 28
    `period unit` IS Days
    `period direction` IS `After the anchor`

`o 19 r 25(1)(b) the period for the notice of appeal after a request for further arguments` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 28
    `period unit` IS Days
    `period direction` IS `After the anchor`

-- The date AFTER WHICH the 28 days run: the date of the lower Court's judgment, or, where a request for further arguments was made
-- under section 29B(2) of the Supreme Court of Judicature Act, the date mentioned in section 29B(4)(b) of that Act (an input).
-- src:2507 | 25. —(1) A party who intends to appeal to the appellate Court against the judgment of the lower Court must file and serve on all parties who have an interest in the appeal a notice of appeal in Form 35 — ( a )
-- src:2508 | within 28 days after the date of the lower Court’s judgment; or
-- src:2509 | ( b )
-- src:2510 | in a case where a request for further arguments has been made under section 29B(2) of the Supreme Court of Judicature Act — within 28 days after the date mentioned in section 29B(4)( b ) of that Act.
-- src:2511 | (2) The appellate Court may extend the time for filing and serving the notice of appeal on the appellant’s application made at any time, and the lower Court may extend the time for filing and serving the notice of appeal if the appellant applies for such extension before the time expires.
@ref O 19 r 25 (src:2507-2511)
GIVEN `a request for further arguments has been made under section 29B(2) of the Supreme Court of Judicature Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the lower Court's judgment` IS A DATE
      `section 29B(4)(b) of the Supreme Court of Judicature Act the date mentioned` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`o 19 r 25(1) the date after which the 28 days for the notice of appeal run` MEANS
    IF `a request for further arguments has been made under section 29B(2) of the Supreme Court of Judicature Act`
    THEN `section 29B(4)(b) of the Supreme Court of Judicature Act the date mentioned` -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the date is in section 29B(4)(b) of the Supreme Court of Judicature Act
    ELSE JUST `the date of the lower Court's judgment`

@ref O 19 r 25(1) (src:2507-2510)
GIVEN `the notice of appeal is in Form 35` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice is served on all parties who have an interest in the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the notice of appeal is filed` IS A DATE
      `the date the notice of appeal is served` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 4 the last day as extended or shortened` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 25(1) the notice of appeal is filed and served as required` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the notice of appeal is in Form 35` AND `the notice is served on all parties who have an interest in the appeal`)
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must file and serve on all parties who have an interest in the appeal a notice of appeal in Form 35"
        IF NOT (`o 19 r 8(3) the filing and the service are done by the last day` `the date the notice of appeal is filed` `the date the notice of appeal is served` `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` `o 3 r 4 the last day as extended or shortened`)
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 28 days after the date of the lower Court’s judgment" -- outside a period the text fixes in its own words
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref O 19 r 25(2) (src:2511)
GIVEN `the appellant applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 25(2) the appellate Court may extend the time for filing and serving the notice of appeal` MEANS
    IF `the appellant applies`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on the appellant’s application made at any time" -- an "on application" that is not met, read as "upon"

@ref O 19 r 25(2) (src:2511)
GIVEN `the appellant applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appellant applies before the time expires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 25(2) the lower Court may extend the time for filing and serving the notice of appeal` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the appellant applies`)
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the appellant applies for such extension" -- an "if" that is not met
        IF `the appellant applies before the time expires`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the lower Court may extend the time ... if the appellant applies for such extension before the time expires" -- an "if" and a time that is not met

