    IF `the appellant has provided security for the respondent's costs of the appeal` AND `the certificate for security for costs in Form 36 is filed` AND `both are done at the time the appellant files the notice of appeal`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The appellant must provide security for the respondent’s costs of the appeal and file a certificate for security for costs in Form 36 at the time the appellant files the notice of appeal"

