§§ `Rule 28 -- related appeals`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:2577 | 28. —(1) Where there are related appeals in the appellate Court, the appellate Court may give directions for the filing and service of such joint documents as may be appropriate in the circumstances. (2) The directions in paragraph (1) may be given by the appellate Court on its own motion or on the application or request of any party to any of the related appeals.
-- src:2578 | (3) To avoid doubt, the appellate Court may give directions under paragraph (1) even if the related appeals comprise one or more appeals filed under this Order and one or more appeals filed under Order 18.
-- src:2579 | (4) Where the related appeals comprise one or more appeals filed under this Order and one or more appeals filed under Order 18, the appellate Court may direct any modifications of the rules that are applicable to an appeal before it, including that the rules of this Division are not to apply to the appeal, and that the rules in Division 5 of Order 18 are to apply instead.
@ref O 19 r 28 (src:2577-2579)
GIVEN `there are related appeals in the appellate Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 28(1) the appellate Court may give directions for the filing and service of joint documents` MEANS
    IF `there are related appeals in the appellate Court`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where there are related appeals in the appellate Court" -- a "where" that is not met

@ref O 19 r 28(2) (src:2577)
GIVEN `the directions are given on the appellate Court's own motion` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directions are given on the application or request of a party to any of the related appeals` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 28(2) the directions in paragraph (1) may be given in this way` MEANS
    IF `the directions are given on the appellate Court's own motion` OR `the directions are given on the application or request of a party to any of the related appeals`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): paragraph (2) names two ways and does not say "only"

@ref O 19 r 28(3) (src:2578)
GIVEN `the related appeals comprise one or more appeals filed under this Order and one or more appeals filed under Order 18` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 28(3) the appellate Court may give directions under paragraph (1) even if the related appeals are of both kinds` MEANS
    IF `the related appeals comprise one or more appeals filed under this Order and one or more appeals filed under Order 18`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (3) speaks only of the case where the related appeals are of both kinds; paragraph (1) covers the rest

@ref O 19 r 28(4) (src:2579)
GIVEN `the related appeals comprise one or more appeals filed under this Order and one or more appeals filed under Order 18` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 28(4) the appellate Court may direct modifications of the rules, including that this Division does not apply and Division 5 of Order 18 applies instead` MEANS
    IF `the related appeals comprise one or more appeals filed under this Order and one or more appeals filed under Order 18`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the related appeals comprise one or more appeals filed under this Order and one or more appeals filed under Order 18" -- a "where" that is not met

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 29 -- appellate Court may specify rules that apply to appeals`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:2581 | 29. —(1) The appellate Court may, if the appellate Court deems appropriate, order that — ( a )
-- src:2582 | this Division, or any part of this Division, does not apply to an appeal before it; and
-- src:2583 | ( b )
-- src:2584 | Division 5 of Order 18, or any part of Division 5 of Order 18, is to apply instead.
-- src:2585 | (2) The appellate Court may in any case if the appellate Court deems appropriate order or direct any modifications of the rules that are applicable to an appeal before it.
-- src:2586 | (3) To avoid doubt, the appellate Court may make an order or give a direction pursuant to this Rule on its own motion.
@ref O 19 r 29 (src:2581-2586)
GIVEN `the appellate Court deems it appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 29(1) the appellate Court may order that this Division, or any part of it, does not apply to an appeal before it, and that Division 5 of Order 18, or any part of it, applies instead` MEANS
    IF `the appellate Court deems it appropriate`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The appellate Court may, if the appellate Court deems appropriate, order that" -- an "if" that is not met

@ref O 19 r 29(2) (src:2585)
GIVEN `the appellate Court deems it appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 29(2) the appellate Court may order or direct modifications of the rules applicable to an appeal before it` MEANS
    IF `the appellate Court deems it appropriate`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The appellate Court may in any case if the appellate Court deems appropriate order or direct any modifications" -- an "if" that is not met

@ref O 19 r 29(3) (src:2586)
GIVEN `the order or direction is made on the appellate Court's own motion` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 29(3) the appellate Court may make an order or give a direction under this Rule` MEANS
    IF `the order or direction is made on the appellate Court's own motion`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "To avoid doubt" the Court may act on its own motion; the text does not say what else may set it going

