`o 19 r 30(3)(a) the appellant must apply in writing to the Registrar to proceed with the appeal and for a copy of the record of proceedings` MEANS
    IF `no written grounds of decision are issued within 12 weeks`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If no written grounds of decision are issued within 12 weeks after the date of filing of the notice of appeal" -- an "if" that is not met

@ref O 19 r 30(3)(b) (src:2592)
GIVEN `no written grounds of decision are issued within 12 weeks` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appellant fails to apply as sub-paragraph (a) requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 30(3)(b) the respondent may apply in writing to the Registrar to proceed or give 14 days' written notice of intention to strike out the appeal` MEANS
    IF `no written grounds of decision are issued within 12 weeks` AND `the appellant fails to apply as sub-paragraph (a) requires`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If no written grounds of decision are issued within 12 weeks ... if the appellant fails to do so" -- an "if" that is not met

@ref O 19 r 30(3)(c) (src:2594)
GIVEN `the respondent has given the appellant 14 days' written notice of intention to strike out the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the 14 days' notice period has expired` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 30(3)(c) the respondent may apply to strike out the appeal` MEANS
    IF `the respondent has given the appellant 14 days' written notice of intention to strike out the appeal` AND `the 14 days' notice period has expired`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "after the expiry of the 14 days’ notice period mentioned in sub‑paragraph ( b ), the respondent may apply to strike out the appeal" -- the notice was not given or its period has not expired

