GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 30(5) the record of appeal filed in the Appellate Division is treated as the record of appeal in the Court of Appeal` MEANS
    IF route's `o 19 r 2 appealed from` EQUALS `Appellate Division` AND route's `o 19 r 2 appealed to` EQUALS `Court of Appeal`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In the case of an appeal to the Court of Appeal against a decision of the Appellate Division" -- a case that is not this one

