-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 31 -- appellant's Case, respondent's Case and appellant's Reply`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `o 19 r 31(1) the appellant's Case` HAS
    `o 19 r 31(1)(a) a succinct summary of the facts, the decision of the lower Court, contentions to be made at the appeal and the orders sought from the appellate Court` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 19 r 31(1)(b) detailed submissions on the facts and the legal issues, including the relevant authorities, highlighting any new points not raised in the lower Court` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 19 r 31(1)(c) references in the right-hand margin to the relevant pages in the record of appeal, the supplemental record of appeal (where required under Rule 30(5)(a)) and the appellant's core bundle of documents` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 19 r 31(1)(d)(i) in the concluding paragraphs, submissions on the appropriate costs orders to be made on appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 19 r 31(1)(d)(ii) in the concluding paragraphs, submissions on the amount of costs and disbursements that should be awarded in respect of all parties to the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 19 r 31(1)(e) the name and signature of the appellant's solicitor` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:2660 | 31. —(1) The appellant’s Case must contain the following: ( a )
-- src:2661 | a succinct summary of the facts, the decision of the lower Court, contentions to be made at the appeal and the orders sought from the appellate Court;
-- src:2662 | ( b )
-- src:2663 | detailed submissions on the facts and the legal issues, including the relevant authorities, highlighting any new points not raised in the lower Court;
-- src:2664 | ( c )
-- src:2665 | references in the right‑hand margin to the relevant pages in the record of appeal, the supplemental record of appeal (where required under Rule 30(5)( a )) and the appellant’s core bundle of documents;
-- src:2666 | ( d )
-- src:2667 | in the concluding paragraphs of the appellant’s Case — (i)
-- src:2668 | submissions on the appropriate costs orders to be made on appeal; and
-- src:2669 | (ii)
-- src:2670 | submissions on the amount of costs and disbursements that should be awarded in respect of all parties to the appeal;
-- src:2671 | ( e )
-- src:2672 | the name and signature of the appellant’s solicitor.
-- src:2673 | (2) The respondent’s Case must contain the following: ( a )
-- src:2674 | a succinct summary of the contentions to be made at the appeal and the orders sought from the appellate Court;
-- src:2675 | ( b )
-- src:2676 | detailed submissions on the facts and the legal issues, including the relevant authorities, highlighting any new points not raised in the lower Court;
-- src:2677 | ( c )
-- src:2678 | references in the right‑hand margin to the relevant pages in the record of appeal, the supplemental record of appeal (where required under Rule 30(5)( a )) and the respondent’s core bundle of documents (if any);
-- src:2679 | ( d )
-- src:2680 | if the respondent intends to submit that — (i)
-- src:2681 | the lower Court’s decision should be varied should the appeal be wholly or partially allowed where the respondent has not appealed against the decision of the lower Court; or
-- src:2682 | (ii)
-- src:2683 | the lower Court’s decision should be affirmed on grounds other than those relied upon by that Court,
-- src:2684 | those submissions and the reasons for the respondent’s submissions;
-- src:2685 | ( e )
-- src:2686 | in the concluding paragraphs of the respondent’s Case — (i)
-- src:2687 | submissions on the appropriate costs orders to be made on appeal; and
-- src:2688 | (ii)
-- src:2689 | submissions on the amount of costs and disbursements that should be awarded in respect of all parties to the appeal;
-- src:2690 | ( f )
-- src:2691 | name and signature of the respondent’s solicitor.
-- src:2692 | (3) Where the respondent fails to comply with the requirements in paragraph (2)( d ), the respondent is not allowed to make the submissions mentioned in paragraph (2)( d ) unless the Court otherwise orders.
-- src:2693 | (4) The appellant’s Reply (if any) must contain the following: ( a )
-- src:2694 | the appellant’s detailed submissions in reply to the respondent’s submissions;
-- src:2695 | ( b )
-- src:2696 | references in the right‑hand margin to the relevant pages in the record of appeal, the supplemental record of appeal (where required under Rule 30(5)( a )), the appellant’s core bundle of documents, the respondent’s core bundle of documents (if any), and the second core bundle (if any);
-- src:2697 | ( c )
-- src:2698 | the name and signature of the appellant’s solicitor.
-- src:2699 | (5) The appellant’s Case, the respondent’s Case and the appellant’s Reply must contain everything that the parties intend to put forward at the appeal and must be prepared on the basis that there will be no need to supplement or to elaborate on any points made.
@ref O 19 r 31 (src:2660-2699)
GIVEN case IS AN `o 19 r 31(1) the appellant's Case`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 31(1) the appellant's Case contains what it must contain` MEANS
    IF    case's `o 19 r 31(1)(a) a succinct summary of the facts, the decision of the lower Court, contentions to be made at the appeal and the orders sought from the appellate Court`
      AND case's `o 19 r 31(1)(b) detailed submissions on the facts and the legal issues, including the relevant authorities, highlighting any new points not raised in the lower Court`
      AND case's `o 19 r 31(1)(c) references in the right-hand margin to the relevant pages in the record of appeal, the supplemental record of appeal (where required under Rule 30(5)(a)) and the appellant's core bundle of documents`
      AND case's `o 19 r 31(1)(d)(i) in the concluding paragraphs, submissions on the appropriate costs orders to be made on appeal`
      AND case's `o 19 r 31(1)(d)(ii) in the concluding paragraphs, submissions on the amount of costs and disbursements that should be awarded in respect of all parties to the appeal`
      AND case's `o 19 r 31(1)(e) the name and signature of the appellant's solicitor`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The appellant’s Case must contain the following"

