-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 32 -- page limits`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `o 19 r 32(1) document` IS ONE OF
    `o 19 r 32(1)(a) the appellant's Case`
    `o 19 r 32(1)(b) the respondent's Case`
    `o 19 r 32(1)(c) the appellant's Reply`

DECLARE `o 19 r 32(2) document` IS ONE OF
    `o 19 r 32(2)(a) the appellant's core bundle of documents (excluding the written judgment or grounds of decision of the lower Court and the extracted order of the lower Court)`
    `o 19 r 32(2)(b) the respondent's core bundle of documents`
    `o 19 r 32(2)(c) the second core bundle`

-- The limits, as a ruler: Case 55, Case 55, Reply 25; core bundles 55, 35, 25.
-- src:2701 | 32. —(1) The appellant’s Case, the respondent’s Case and the appellant’s Reply (if any) are subject to the following page limits, unless the appellate Court otherwise orders: ( a )
-- src:2702 | appellant’s Case — 55 pages;
-- src:2703 | ( b )
-- src:2704 | respondent’s Case — 55 pages;
-- src:2705 | ( c )
-- src:2706 | appellant’s Reply — 25 pages.
-- src:2707 | (2) The appellant’s core bundle of documents (excluding the written judgment or grounds of decision of the lower Court and the extracted order of the lower Court), the respondent’s core bundle of documents and the second core bundle are subject to the following page limits, unless the appellate Court otherwise orders: ( a )
-- src:2708 | appellant’s core bundle of documents (excluding the written judgment or grounds of decision of the lower Court and the extracted order of the lower Court) — 55 pages;
-- src:2709 | ( b )
-- src:2710 | respondent’s core bundle of documents — 35 pages;
-- src:2711 | ( c )
-- src:2712 | second core bundle — 25 pages.
-- src:2713 | (3) The appellate Court may allow the page limit mentioned in paragraphs (1) and (2) to be exceeded — ( a )
-- src:2714 | in special circumstances; and
-- src:2715 | ( b )
-- src:2716 | unless the appellate Court otherwise orders under paragraph (4), upon the payment of the fees and additional fees prescribed for the filing of pages in excess of the page limit.
-- src:2717 | (4) The appellate Court may upon application waive, refund, defer or apportion the payment of the fees mentioned in paragraph (3)( b ).
@ref O 19 r 32 (src:2701-2717)
GIVEN document IS A `o 19 r 32(1) document`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`o 19 r 32(1) the page limit` MEANS
    CONSIDER document
    WHEN `o 19 r 32(1)(a) the appellant's Case` THEN 55
    WHEN `o 19 r 32(1)(b) the respondent's Case` THEN 55
    WHEN `o 19 r 32(1)(c) the appellant's Reply` THEN 25

@ref O 19 r 32(1) (src:2701-2706)
GIVEN document IS A `o 19 r 32(1) document`
      pages IS A NUMBER
      `the appellate Court otherwise orders` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 32(1) the document is within the page limit` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the appellate Court otherwise orders`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "unless the appellate Court otherwise orders" -- the order's limit is not in these sources
        IF pages AT MOST `o 19 r 32(1) the page limit` document
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "are subject to the following page limits ... appellant’s Case — 55 pages; respondent’s Case — 55 pages; appellant’s Reply — 25 pages"

@ref O 19 r 32(2) (src:2707-2712)
GIVEN document IS A `o 19 r 32(2) document`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`o 19 r 32(2) the page limit` MEANS
    CONSIDER document
    WHEN `o 19 r 32(2)(a) the appellant's core bundle of documents (excluding the written judgment or grounds of decision of the lower Court and the extracted order of the lower Court)` THEN 55
    WHEN `o 19 r 32(2)(b) the respondent's core bundle of documents` THEN 35
    WHEN `o 19 r 32(2)(c) the second core bundle` THEN 25

@ref O 19 r 32(2) (src:2707-2712)
GIVEN document IS A `o 19 r 32(2) document`
