-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 33 -- payment out of security for costs and release of undertaking`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:2719 | 33. —(1) This Rule applies without the need for an order from the Court. (2) Where costs are payable by the appellant to the respondent under any order made by the appellate Court, the security for costs provided under Rule 27 must be paid to the respondent towards the costs ordered and the balance (if any) of the security must be paid to the appellant.
-- src:2720 | (3) Where no costs are payable by the appellant to the respondent under any order made by the appellate Court, the security for costs provided under Rule 27 must be paid to the appellant and the appellant’s solicitor is released from any undertaking as to the costs for the appeal.
-- src:2721 | (4) Paragraphs (2) and (3) apply with necessary modifications to the payment out of security for costs given under Rule 35(6).
@ref O 19 r 33 (src:2719-2721)
GIVEN `the Court has made an order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 33(1) an order from the Court is needed for this Rule to apply` MEANS
    JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This Rule applies without the need for an order from the Court" -- whether or not the Court has made one

@ref O 19 r 33(2) (src:2719)
GIVEN `the costs payable by the appellant to the respondent under an order made by the appellate Court` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 33(2) the security for costs must be paid to the respondent towards the costs ordered` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the costs payable by the appellant to the respondent under an order made by the appellate Court`
    WHEN JUST costs THEN
        IF costs GREATER THAN 0
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where costs are payable by the appellant to the respondent" -- none are payable
    WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where costs are payable by the appellant to the respondent" -- none are payable

-- The amount paid to the respondent is the smaller of the costs ordered and the security; the balance goes to the appellant.
-- By paragraph (4) the same arithmetic serves the security given under Rule 35(6), so the input is named for both.
@ref O 19 r 33(2) (src:2719)
GIVEN `the security for costs provided under Rule 27 or, by paragraph (4), under Rule 35(6)` IS A NUMBER
      `the costs payable by the appellant to the respondent under an order made by the appellate Court` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`o 19 r 33(2) the amount of the security paid to the respondent` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the costs payable by the appellant to the respondent under an order made by the appellate Court`
    WHEN JUST costs THEN
        BRANCH
            IF costs AT MOST 0
                THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no costs are payable, so paragraph (3) applies
            IF costs AT MOST `the security for costs provided under Rule 27 or, by paragraph (4), under Rule 35(6)`
                THEN JUST costs
            OTHERWISE JUST `the security for costs provided under Rule 27 or, by paragraph (4), under Rule 35(6)`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no costs are payable, so paragraph (3) applies

@ref O 19 r 33(2) (src:2719)
GIVEN `the security for costs provided under Rule 27 or, by paragraph (4), under Rule 35(6)` IS A NUMBER
      `the costs payable by the appellant to the respondent under an order made by the appellate Court` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`o 19 r 33(2) the balance of the security paid to the appellant` MEANS
    CONSIDER `o 19 r 33(2) the amount of the security paid to the respondent` `the security for costs provided under Rule 27 or, by paragraph (4), under Rule 35(6)` `the costs payable by the appellant to the respondent under an order made by the appellate Court`
    WHEN JUST paid THEN JUST (`the security for costs provided under Rule 27 or, by paragraph (4), under Rule 35(6)` MINUS paid)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no costs are payable, so paragraph (3) applies

