    `period length` IS 14
    `period unit` IS Days
    `period direction` IS `After the anchor`

-- src:2746 | 36. An application for the permission of — ( a )
-- src:2747 | a Judge sitting in the Appellate Division under section 40(4)( b ) of the Supreme Court of Judicature Act, to make an application to discharge or vary any direction or order mentioned in section 40(4)( a ) of that Act; or
-- src:2748 | ( b )
-- src:2749 | a Judge sitting in the Court of Appeal under section 58(4)( b ) of the Supreme Court of Judicature Act, to make an application to discharge or vary any direction or order mentioned in section 58(4)( a ) of that Act,
-- src:2750 | must be filed and served on all parties who have an interest in the appeal within 14 days after the date on which that direction or order is made.
@ref O 19 r 36 (src:2746-2750)
GIVEN `the application is for the permission of a Judge sitting in the Appellate Division under section 40(4)(b), or of a Judge sitting in the Court of Appeal under section 58(4)(b), of the Supreme Court of Judicature Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is filed and served on all parties who have an interest in the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the application is filed` IS A DATE
      `the date the application is served` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 4 the last day as extended or shortened` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 36 the application for permission is filed and served as required` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the application is for the permission of a Judge sitting in the Appellate Division under section 40(4)(b), or of a Judge sitting in the Court of Appeal under section 58(4)(b), of the Supreme Court of Judicature Act`)
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): rule 36 speaks only of an application for permission under section 40(4)(b) or 58(4)(b)
        IF NOT (`the application is filed and served on all parties who have an interest in the appeal`)
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be filed and served on all parties who have an interest in the appeal"
        IF NOT (`o 19 r 8(3) the filing and the service are done by the last day` `the date the application is filed` `the date the application is served` `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` `o 3 r 4 the last day as extended or shortened`)
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 14 days after the date on which that direction or order is made" -- outside a period the text fixes in its own words
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 37 -- written submissions for applications to the appellate Court`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

`o 19 r 37(1) the period for the written submissions and the bundle of authorities` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 14
    `period unit` IS Days
    `period direction` IS `After the anchor`

-- src:2752 | 37. —(1) Except where otherwise provided by any provision of these Rules or any other written law, or unless the appellate Court otherwise directs, the applicant and the opposing party must file and serve written submissions (if any) as well as any bundle of authorities in respect of an application before the appellate Court within 14 days after the date on which the opposing party’s affidavit in reply is to be filed and served. (2) The written submissions for the application are subject to a page limit of 35 pages, unless the appellate Court otherwise orders.
-- src:2753 | (3) The appellate Court may allow the page limit mentioned in paragraph (2) to be exceeded — ( a )
-- src:2754 | in special circumstances; and
-- src:2755 | ( b )
-- src:2756 | unless the appellate Court otherwise orders under paragraph (4), upon the payment of the fees and additional fees prescribed for the filing of pages in excess of the page limit.
-- src:2757 | (4) The appellate Court may upon application waive, refund, defer or apportion the payment of the fees mentioned in paragraph (3)( b ).
-- src:2758 | (5) There must not be more than one set of submissions for each party or set of parties represented by the same firm of solicitors unless the appellate Court otherwise orders.
-- src:2759 | (6) The concluding paragraphs of the written submissions must include — ( a )
-- src:2760 | submissions on the appropriate costs orders to be made in the application; and
-- src:2761 | ( b )
-- src:2762 | submissions on the amount of costs and disbursements that should be awarded in respect of all parties to the application.
@ref O 19 r 37 (src:2752-2762)
GIVEN `these Rules or any other written law otherwise provide` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appellate Court otherwise directs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party has written submissions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the written submissions and any bundle of authorities are filed and served` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the submissions are filed` IS A DATE
      `the date the submissions are served` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 4 the last day as extended or shortened` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 37(1) the written submissions and the bundle of authorities are filed and served as required` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `these Rules or any other written law otherwise provide`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Except where otherwise provided by any provision of these Rules or any other written law" -- the other provision is not named
        IF `the appellate Court otherwise directs`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "unless the appellate Court otherwise directs" -- what the direction says is not in these sources
        IF NOT (`the party has written submissions`)
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "written submissions (if any)" -- an "if" that is not met (fork F9)
        IF NOT (`the written submissions and any bundle of authorities are filed and served`)
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the applicant and the opposing party must file and serve written submissions (if any) as well as any bundle of authorities"
        IF NOT (`o 19 r 8(3) the filing and the service are done by the last day` `the date the submissions are filed` `the date the submissions are served` `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` `o 3 r 4 the last day as extended or shortened`)
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 14 days after the date on which the opposing party’s affidavit in reply is to be filed and served" -- outside a period the text fixes in its own words
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref O 19 r 37(2) (src:2752)
GIVEN pages IS A NUMBER
      `the appellate Court otherwise orders` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 37(2) the written submissions are within the page limit` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the appellate Court otherwise orders`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "unless the appellate Court otherwise orders" -- the order's limit is not in these sources
        IF pages AT MOST 35
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "subject to a page limit of 35 pages"

@ref O 19 r 37(3) (src:2753-2756)
GIVEN `there are special circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 37(3)(a) the appellate Court may allow the page limit to be exceeded` MEANS
    IF `there are special circumstances`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is given "in special circumstances"

@ref O 19 r 37(3)(b) (src:2755-2756)
GIVEN `the appellate Court allows the page limit to be exceeded` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appellate Court otherwise orders under paragraph (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 37(3)(b) the fees and additional fees for the pages in excess are payable` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the appellate Court allows the page limit to be exceeded`)
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may allow the page limit ... to be exceeded ... upon the payment of the fees" -- an "upon" that is not met
        IF `the appellate Court otherwise orders under paragraph (4)`
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the appellate Court otherwise orders under paragraph (4)"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref O 19 r 37(3)(b) (src:2755-2756)
GIVEN `the appellate Court allows the page limit to be exceeded` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appellate Court otherwise orders under paragraph (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `sch 4 the fee for this document` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`o 19 r 37(3)(b) the amount payable for the pages in excess` MEANS
    IF `o 19 r 37(3)(b) the fees and additional fees for the pages in excess are payable` `the appellate Court allows the page limit to be exceeded` `the appellate Court otherwise orders under paragraph (4)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST `sch 4 the fee for this document`
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the fees are not payable here, or have been waived, refunded, deferred or apportioned, and the amount then is not in these sources

