-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 38 -- powers in sections 40(1) and 58(1) of the Supreme Court of Judicature Act exercisable by the Registrar`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

`o 19 r 38(2) the period for the application to vary or discharge` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 14
    `period unit` IS Days
    `period direction` IS `After the anchor`

DECLARE `o 19 r 38(1) kind of direction or order` IS ONE OF
    `o 19 r 38(1)(a) extension of time to file or serve a record of appeal, a supplemental record of appeal, an appellant's core bundle of documents, an appellant's Case or a respondent's Case`
    `o 19 r 38(1)(b) extension of time to file or serve an appellant's Reply, a respondent's core bundle of documents and an appellant's second core bundle, a bundle of authorities, written submissions or affidavits in an application, or a bundle of documents in an application for permission to appeal`
    `o 19 r 38(1)(c) a direction under Rule 28(1)`
    `o 19 r 38(1)(d) amendment of a document filed for an appeal or application`
    `o 19 r 38(1)(e) expunging a document filed for an appeal or application, and consequential directions`
    `o 19 r 38(1)(f) rescheduling of a hearing`
    `o 19 r 38(1) any other direction or order`

-- src:2764 | 38. —(1) The Registrar may exercise the powers of the Appellate Division and the Court of Appeal in sections 40(1)( a ) and 58(1)( a ) of the Supreme Court of Judicature Act in the following circumstances: ( a )
-- src:2765 | where the direction or order is for the extension of time to file or serve a record of appeal, a supplemental record of appeal, an appellant’s core bundle of documents, an appellant’s Case or a respondent’s Case, and all of the parties consent to the making of the direction or order;
-- src:2766 | ( b )
-- src:2767 | where the direction or order is for the extension of time to file or serve any of the following documents: (i)
-- src:2768 | an appellant’s Reply;
-- src:2769 | (ii)
-- src:2770 | a respondent’s core bundle of documents and an appellant’s second core bundle;
-- src:2771 | (iii)
-- src:2772 | a bundle of authorities in any appeal or application;
-- src:2773 | (iv)
-- src:2774 | written submissions or affidavits in any application;
-- src:2775 | (v)
-- src:2776 | a bundle of documents in any application for permission to appeal;
-- src:2777 | ( c )
-- src:2778 | where the direction is a direction under Rule 28(1);
-- src:2779 | ( d )
-- src:2780 | where the direction or order is for the amendment of any document filed for any appeal or application, and all of the parties consent to the making of the direction or order;
-- src:2781 | ( e )
-- src:2782 | where the direction or order relates to expunging any document filed for any appeal or application, and all of the parties consent to the making of the direction or order, and for consequential directions in relation to the direction or order;
-- src:2783 | ( f )
-- src:2784 | where the direction or order relates to the rescheduling of any hearing.
-- src:2785 | (2) An application to vary or discharge any direction or order of the Registrar under paragraph (1) may be made to a single Judge sitting in the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal (as the case may be), and any such application must be filed and served on all parties who have an interest in the appeal within 14 days after the date on which that direction or order is made, and the decision of that Judge is final.
@ref O 19 r 38 (src:2764-2785)
GIVEN kind IS A `o 19 r 38(1) kind of direction or order`
      `all of the parties consent to the making of the direction or order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 38(1) the Registrar may exercise the powers of the Appellate Division and the Court of Appeal in sections 40(1)(a) and 58(1)(a) of the Supreme Court of Judicature Act` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `o 19 r 38(1)(a) extension of time to file or serve a record of appeal, a supplemental record of appeal, an appellant's core bundle of documents, an appellant's Case or a respondent's Case` THEN
        IF `all of the parties consent to the making of the direction or order`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "and all of the parties consent to the making of the direction or order" -- the consent is missing
    WHEN `o 19 r 38(1)(b) extension of time to file or serve an appellant's Reply, a respondent's core bundle of documents and an appellant's second core bundle, a bundle of authorities, written submissions or affidavits in an application, or a bundle of documents in an application for permission to appeal` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 19 r 38(1)(c) a direction under Rule 28(1)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 19 r 38(1)(d) amendment of a document filed for an appeal or application` THEN
        IF `all of the parties consent to the making of the direction or order`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "and all of the parties consent to the making of the direction or order" -- the consent is missing
    WHEN `o 19 r 38(1)(e) expunging a document filed for an appeal or application, and consequential directions` THEN
        IF `all of the parties consent to the making of the direction or order`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "and all of the parties consent to the making of the direction or order" -- the consent is missing
    WHEN `o 19 r 38(1)(f) rescheduling of a hearing` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 19 r 38(1) any other direction or order` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): rule 38(1) lists six circumstances and does not say "only"

@ref O 19 r 38(2) (src:2785)
GIVEN `the direction or order is a direction or order of the Registrar under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 38(2) an application to vary or discharge may be made to a single Judge sitting in the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal` MEANS
    IF `the direction or order is a direction or order of the Registrar under paragraph (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (2) speaks only of "any direction or order of the Registrar under paragraph (1)"

@ref O 19 r 38(2) (src:2785)
GIVEN `the application is to vary or discharge a direction or order of the Registrar under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is filed and served on all parties who have an interest in the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the application is filed` IS A DATE
      `the date the application is served` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 4 the last day as extended or shortened` IS A MAYBE DATE
