`o 19 r 38(2) the application to vary or discharge is filed and served as required` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the application is to vary or discharge a direction or order of the Registrar under paragraph (1)`)
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (2) speaks only of an application "to vary or discharge any direction or order of the Registrar under paragraph (1)"
        IF NOT (`the application is filed and served on all parties who have an interest in the appeal`)
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be filed and served on all parties who have an interest in the appeal"
        IF NOT (`o 19 r 8(3) the filing and the service are done by the last day` `the date the application is filed` `the date the application is served` `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` `o 3 r 4 the last day as extended or shortened`)
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 14 days after the date on which that direction or order is made" -- outside a period the text fixes in its own words
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref O 19 r 38(2) (src:2785)
GIVEN `the decision is that of the single Judge on an application under paragraph (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
