`o 19 r 39(5) the Court of Appeal may have regard to the matter` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the Court of Appeal is determining whether it is more appropriate for it to hear an appeal that has been made to the Appellate Division`)
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "when determining whether it is more appropriate for the Court of Appeal to hear an appeal that has been made to the Appellate Division" -- a "when" that is not met
        IF matter EQUALS `o 19 r 39(5)(g) any other relevant matter` AND NOT (`the matter is relevant`)
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any other relevant matter" -- this matter is not relevant, and the text says nothing of an irrelevant one
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 40 -- transfer of appeal from the Court of Appeal to the Appellate Division`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

`o 19 r 40(2)(b) the period for the application on the ground in section 29E(2)(b)` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 14
    `period unit` IS Days
    `period direction` IS `After the anchor`

DECLARE `o 19 r 40(1) matter` IS ONE OF
    `o 19 r 40(1)(a) the appeal was not made to the Court of Appeal in accordance with section 29C of the Supreme Court of Judicature Act`
    `o 19 r 40(1)(b) none of the legal issues raised on appeal engage any of the matters set out in the Sixth Schedule to the Supreme Court of Judicature Act`
    `o 19 r 40(1)(c) all of the legal issues raised on appeal in relation to the matters set out in the Sixth Schedule relate to issues of settled law`
    `o 19 r 40(1) any other matter`

-- src:2810 | 40. —(1) For the purposes of section 29E(3) of the Supreme Court of Judicature Act, the Court of Appeal is to have regard to the following matters, in deciding whether to exercise the power in section 29E(1) of that Act on its own motion, to transfer to the Appellate Division an appeal against a decision of the General Division that has been made to the Court of Appeal: ( a )
-- src:2811 | the appeal was not made to the Court of Appeal in accordance with section 29C of that Act;
-- src:2812 | ( b )
-- src:2813 | none of the legal issues raised on appeal engage any of the matters set out in the Sixth Schedule to that Act;
-- src:2814 | ( c )
-- src:2815 | all of the legal issues raised on appeal in relation to the matters set out in the Sixth Schedule to that Act relate to issues of settled law.
-- src:2816 | (2) An application under section 29E(2)( b ) of the Supreme Court of Judicature Act to transfer to the Appellate Division an appeal against a decision of the General Division that has been made to the Court of Appeal — ( a )
-- src:2817 | must be made in accordance with Rule 35; and
-- src:2818 | ( b )
-- src:2819 | must be filed and served within 14 days after the date of service of the notice of appeal on all parties who have an interest in the appeal.
@ref O 19 r 40 (src:2810-2819)
GIVEN matter IS A `o 19 r 40(1) matter`
      `the Court of Appeal is deciding, on its own motion, whether to exercise the power in section 29E(1) of the Supreme Court of Judicature Act to transfer to the Appellate Division an appeal against a decision of the General Division that has been made to the Court of Appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 40(1) the Court of Appeal is to have regard to the matter` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the Court of Appeal is deciding, on its own motion, whether to exercise the power in section 29E(1) of the Supreme Court of Judicature Act to transfer to the Appellate Division an appeal against a decision of the General Division that has been made to the Court of Appeal`)
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in deciding whether to exercise the power in section 29E(1) of that Act on its own motion" -- a deciding that is not this one
        IF matter EQUALS `o 19 r 40(1) any other matter`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): rule 40(1) lists three matters and does not say "only"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref O 19 r 40(2) (src:2816-2819)
GIVEN `the application is under section 29E(2)(b) of the Supreme Court of Judicature Act to transfer to the Appellate Division an appeal against a decision of the General Division that has been made to the Court of Appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is made in accordance with Rule 35` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is filed and served` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the application is filed` IS A DATE
      `the date the application is served` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 4 the last day as extended or shortened` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 40(2) the application under section 29E(2)(b) is made, filed and served as required` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the application is under section 29E(2)(b) of the Supreme Court of Judicature Act to transfer to the Appellate Division an appeal against a decision of the General Division that has been made to the Court of Appeal`)
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (2) speaks only of "An application under section 29E(2)( b )"
        IF NOT (`the application is made in accordance with Rule 35` AND `the application is filed and served`)
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be made in accordance with Rule 35; and must be filed and served"
        IF NOT (`o 19 r 8(3) the filing and the service are done by the last day` `the date the application is filed` `the date the application is served` `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` `o 3 r 4 the last day as extended or shortened`)
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 14 days after the date of service of the notice of appeal on all parties who have an interest in the appeal" -- outside a period the text fixes in its own words
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

